WEBVTT

1
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Whoever gets to the temple first win!

2
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.000
What?

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Aang, no fair!

4
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Let's get him!

5
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Hurry up!

6
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.000
- Hi, Nima.
- Good morning, Aang.

7
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
- Hei, mipmip.
- Oh, hello, Aang.

8
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Oh, perfect timing.

9
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.000
I don't mind giving me a lift.

10
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Gyatso, this isn't the best time.

11
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.000
I'm getting old, you know.

12
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.000
My body doesn't move like it used to.

13
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.000
I'm kind of in the middle of something.

14
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.000
You are so heavy.

15
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Heavy? Me?

16
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
I eat nothing but vegetables.

17
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Pie is not a vegetable.

18
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.000
I'm gonna lose the race.

19
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Race? What race?

20
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.000
We finally won!

21
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.000
We won! We won!

22
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Aang,

23
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.000
as an airbender,

24
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
it's important that you
know when to show restraint.

25
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Even if you have the power to win,

26
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.000
you are the Avatar.

27
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.000
A lot of people are going to rely on you.

28
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.000
He's gone!

29
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.000
He ran away!

30
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.000
What? I'm here!

31
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Where's the Avatar?

32
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.000
Avatar!

33
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Aang, where are you?

34
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Gyatso, I'm here!

35
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.000
I'm right here!

36
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.000
I'm here!

37
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.000
I'm here.

38
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Hi, Momo.

39
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Hi, Appa.

40
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.000
Was I asleep for long?

41
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Ooh! Okay, okay.

42
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
I'm awake already.

43
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.000
I know, I know.

44
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.000
We've got a job to finish.

45
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Let's continue our journey.

46
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Back to our old home.

47
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.000
This may not have been our best trip,

48
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.000
but any Airbender relic we
find makes it all worthwhile.

49
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.000
This could be the oldest
piece in our collection.

50
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Sonum.

51
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.000
I miss you.

52
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Momo, go outside with Appa.

53
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.000
Now!

54
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.000
Who are you?

55
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.000
Why are you doing this?

56
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.000
Please, Stop.

57
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.000
I don't want to hurt you.

58
00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.000
Where is it?

59
00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.000
No, that's not it.

60
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.000
Hey, those are antiques.

61
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.000
Enough!

62
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.000
Wait!

63
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.000
I found it!

64
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Sonum, why an after you?

65
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Wait!

66
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.000
No, that's 1,000 years old!

67
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
Why don't we just talk?
Maybe I can help.

68
00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.000
We don't need your help, Avatar.

69
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.000
We're done living in a world where benders
have all the power and we have none.

70
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.000
Who are you?

71
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.000
We're the Denied.

72
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.000
The Denied?

73
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.000
Just kill him already!

74
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.000
No! He'll bring the whole place down!

75
00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.000
You saved me.

76
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.000
Kalik, wrap the map! Let's go!

77
00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Oh, no!

78
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.000
I'm fine.

79
00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.000
Momo, I'm fine.

80
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.000
We've got to get to Republic City.

81
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Appa, yip, yip!

82
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.000
Water,

83
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.000
her tribes gather strength
from the moon

84
00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.000
and flow with the tides.

85
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Earth,

86
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.000
a kingdomof unshakable will.

87
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Reliable and strong.

88
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.000
Fire,

89
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.000
a nation capable
of great destruction,

90
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:52.000
but also of great warmth.

91
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
Air,

92
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.000
peaceful nomads with
the power of a hurricane,

93
00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.000
but the spirit of a gentle breeze.

94
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.000
For generations, the Avatar,

95
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:11.000
the one master of all four elements,
kept the nations in balance.

96
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:17.000
But when that responsibility
fell to me as a child, I ran away.

97
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.000
I was caught in a deadly storm,

98
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.000
but my Avatar spirit preserved
me in a sphere of energy

99
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.000
where I stayed for 100 years.

100
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.000
I woke to discover that the
balance preserved by the Avatar

101
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
had been destroyed by war.

102
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.000
The air nomads were gone.

103
00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.000
All but one.

104
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.000
Me.

105
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:45.000
I could no longer run for my
responsibility as the Avatar.

106
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.000
I found allies from every nation.

107
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:52.000
Benders and non-benders.

108
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.000
Katara taught me how to waterbend.

109
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:59.000
Toph trained me in the
ways of the earthbenders.

110
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:04.000
Zuko, once my worst enemy,
became my firebending teacher.

111
00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:09.000
Sokka showed me that bravery is the
most important part of being a leader.

112
00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.000
We became a family.

113
00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:17.000
And together,
we ended the Hundred Year War.

114
00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:23.000
Then, we began the hard
work of rebuilding the world.

115
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.000
For so long,
the nations stood apart, alone,

116
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:40.000
and we all suffered as a result.

117
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:43.000
But here, on this ancient site,

118
00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:46.000
we created a place where all people are
welcome,

119
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.000
bender and non-bender alike,

120
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:52.000
working together in
peace to build the future.

121
00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.000
Though there are still those
who would seek to divide us,

122
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.000
we remain united.

123
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.000
As a council representative,

124
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.000
I am honored to be here today celebrating
the anniversary of Republic City

125
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:11.000
and the opening of Unity Tower,
a symbol for all people.

126
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.000
Yeah!

127
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.000
It's the Avatar!

128
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.000
Momo!

129
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.000
Appa!

130
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.000
I missed you, too, old friend.

131
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.000
Aang!

132
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.000
Katara!

133
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.000
You're hurt.

134
00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.000
Take a deep breath,

135
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:04.000
and exhale.

136
00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.000
I've heard the Denied
are growing in numbers,

137
00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.000
but they've never done anything like this.

138
00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.000
Attacking the Avatar?

139
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.000
Yeah.

140
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.000
They were incredible fighters,

141
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.000
even without bending.

142
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.000
Ahh, Ow!

143
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.000
Oops!

144
00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.000
Breathe through it.

145
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.000
Be honest. You're enjoying this.

146
00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Aang, this is serious.

147
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.000
Whatever this map they took was,

148
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:29.000
if they were willing
to kill the Avatar to get it,

149
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.000
what else are they willing to do?

150
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.000
I don't know.

151
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.000
I'm worried about you.

152
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.000
You're spending more and
more time at the Air Temple, alone.

153
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:44.000
It's how I hold on to my past.

154
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.000
I know how hard this is for you.

155
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.000
When I was attacked,

156
00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.000
all I could think about was that...

157
00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.000
this could be it.

158
00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.000
I'm the last Airbender.

159
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.000
If I die,

160
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.000
my culture dies with me.

161
00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.000
You may be the last Airbender,

162
00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:16.000
but you're not alone.

163
00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.000
Aang,

164
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.000
None of this would exist without you.

165
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:25.000
You made the city possible
with your heart and your mind.

166
00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.000
Because of you,

167
00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:31.000
all of the nations live here, together.

168
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.000
All except mine.

169
00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:50.000
I know, but the people here
still need your protection.

170
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.000
You're an Airbender,

171
00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.000
but you're also the Avatar.

172
00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.000
You're right.

173
00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:04.000
Whoever this Sonum person is,
I need to find out more.

174
00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.000
Aang.

175
00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.000
Avatar Roku.

176
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.000
It is good to see you again.

177
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.000
How can I help you?

178
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:40.000
In your lifetime, did you ever hear of
an ancient Airbender named Sonum?

179
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:44.000
I have not,
but you have many past lives to call upon.

180
00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:49.000
Perhaps one further back in
the Avatar cycle can help you.

181
00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.000
Thank you, Avatar Roku.

182
00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.000
- I'm sorry.
- I've never heard of Sonum.

183
00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.000
- Perhaps earlier.
- You must go find him.

184
00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.000
Not here. Not here.

185
00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:11.000
Um, hello?

186
00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:14.000
Is there anyone here?

187
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.000
Hello?

188
00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:23.000
Who calls upon Avatar Xion,
vast wealth of knowledge

189
00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.000
Oh, hello.

190
00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:32.000
You look like an Avatar from
a time quite distant from mine.

191
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:35.000
Please, please,
tell me about your era.

192
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.000
What are people wearing?

193
00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.000
Are sandals still a thing?

194
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.000
Uh, yes.

195
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Why? Why?

196
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:48.000
After so many years, open toes,
in someone else's crusty cuticles.

197
00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.000
Disgusting.

198
00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:50.000
Right.

199
00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.000
Anyway, I have come through guidance.

200
00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.000
You see, I was attacked.

201
00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:56.000
It was not me, okay?
It wasn't me.

202
00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.000
I know that.

203
00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:01.000
I think it might have something to do
with an Airbender named Sonum.

204
00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:04.000
Sonum. It sounds familiar.

205
00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.000
Sonum.
Where have I heard that name before?

206
00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:12.000
Sonum was the youngest daughter of the owner of
the possum chicken shop at the corner marketplace.

207
00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:15.000
Wait. That was my ex, Soniam.

208
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.000
If only she didn't have
those humongous toenails.

209
00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.000
Ugh. Disgusting.

210
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.000
This is going nowhere.

211
00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
Sonum?

212
00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:26.000
Well, thank you for your time.

213
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.000
I must continue my search.

214
00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.000
Oh! Sonum!

215
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.000
You're asking about the
legend of the lost Avatar.

216
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.000
Sona m was an Avatar?

217
00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.000
Indeed she was.

218
00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:42.000
She was the Avatar in the
golden age of Airbender.

219
00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:48.000
Legend said she had a staff that could
channel the vast energy of the spirit world,

220
00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.000
granting its keeper unlimited power.

221
00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:55.000
Is... Is that even possible?

222
00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.000
We'll never know for sure.

223
00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:00.000
Many Avatars have tried to
communicate with her, but they couldn't.

224
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.000
She disappeared so completely
that it was as if she never existed.

225
00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.000
And perhaps it's better that way.

226
00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:12.000
Maybe such a staff was too
dangerous for anyone to possess.

227
00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.000
Even the Avatar.

228
00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:17.000
But... But that's exactly
why I need to find it.

229
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:20.000
The people who attacked
me discovered a map.

230
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.000
It must lead to the staff.

231
00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:24.000
Avatar Xion, please.

232
00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:27.000
You have to tell me where it is.

233
00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:35.000
The legend says that Sonum disappeared
with her staff on the peak of Mount Baihu.

234
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:40.000
Katara, I'm sorry to leave so suddenly,

235
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.000
but I found out what the Denied are after.

236
00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.000
Sonim had a staff of immense power.

237
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.000
And in their hands, it could
be a devastating weapon.

238
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.000
They have a head start.

239
00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.000
There's no time to waste.

240
00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:57.000
You take Appa and Momo and
gather up the rest of the team.

241
00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.000
We're gonna need some help.

242
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:08.000
Next on the agenda,
a Fire Nation naval vessel

243
00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:12.000
came into conflict with an extremist
group of non-Benders called the Denied.

244
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.000
They've been
robbing ancient sites...

245
00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.000
Your Majesty!

246
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.000
An urgent message has
arrived from Republic City.

247
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:19.000
How impudent.

248
00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:20.000
Can't you see Fire Lord Zuko is...

249
00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:23.000
Chamberlain.

250
00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.000
There's only one person
who can send a message

251
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.000
urgent enough to interrupt
the Fire Lord's counsel.

252
00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.000
Is it from the Avatar?

253
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:32.000
Yes, my lord.

254
00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.000
Um...

255
00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:37.000
What are you doing?

256
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.000
Read it quickly.

257
00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:42.000
Uh, y-y-yes, Grand Chamberlain.

258
00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.000
Flameo Hartman,
house ruling the Fire Nation.

259
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.000
I hope the boring Chamberlain
you mentioned...

260
00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:51.000
in your letters isn't
still annoying you.

261
00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.000
Anywho, to cut to the
chase, I need your help.

262
00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:57.000
Can you please come immediately?

263
00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:01.000
Oh, and don't forget to
bring some firecracker buns.

264
00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:06.000
Allow me to present Sokka Cycle.

265
00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:10.000
Flames launch you into the sky where
you can drop water bombs on your enemies.

266
00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.000
Then skis pop out to
help you stick the landing.

267
00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.000
Pretty great, right?

268
00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.000
Eh, boring.

269
00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.000
Why would you need a sled
when you can just waterbend?

270
00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.000
Oh, oh, oh, like me, like me!

271
00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.000
Whee!

272
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:24.000
Keep in mind, there's still plenty
of folks like me who can't bend.

273
00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.000
Why would Avatar Aang
partner with a non-bender?

274
00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:28.000
Ugh. Why?

275
00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.000
I'll tell you why.

276
00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.000
I saved him from the iceberg.

277
00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:36.000
My boomerang flew by his side while I
carried away enemies with my trusty blade.

278
00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:39.000
I even took down the whole
Fire Nation airship armada.

279
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:44.000
And on top of all that, I
was more popular than him.

280
00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.000
You're such a liar, Sokka.

281
00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.000
It's from the Avatar.

282
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.000
Really?

283
00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.000
Cool!

284
00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.000
Oh, so now you think I'm cool?

285
00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.000
All right, metalbenders.

286
00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.000
Let's see if any of you tenderfoots

287
00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.000
can at least make me use my hands.

288
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:39.000
I'm still the greatest
earthbender in the world!

289
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.000
And I'm bored.

290
00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.000
M-Master Toph,
there's a bird on your head.

291
00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.000
And?

292
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.000
It looks like it has a message.

293
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.000
Read.

294
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:49.000
Uh, it's from Avatar Aang.

295
00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.000
He needs your help.

296
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.000
It's the Denied?

297
00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.000
Where is he?

298
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.000
Mount Bihu.

299
00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.000
No, no, no!

300
00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.000
No.

301
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.000
I love that hat.

302
00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.000
Sonum?

303
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:58.000
Could that be you?

304
00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.000
Who are you?

305
00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:56.000
Aang!

306
00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:26.000
Team avatar to the rescue.

307
00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:29.000
Aang.

308
00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:30.000
You made it.

309
00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:33.000
You couldn't wait a day before
running off to get yourself killed?

310
00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:35.000
I thought you were
here to looking for staff.

311
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:37.000
Who is this guy?

312
00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:46.000
It Airbender

313
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.000
How did he hold up an entire mountain?

314
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:12.000
His chi is strong,
like nothing I've ever felt.

315
00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:18.000
Hey, Avatar, you think this guy beat
your record for longest frozen airbender?

316
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:21.000
Yeah.
How long do you think he was in that ice?

317
00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:26.000
I don't know. His tattoos look ancient.

318
00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:28.000
He's been in there a long time.

319
00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:29.000
He smells good for an old guy.

320
00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:30.000
Ew.

321
00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.000
What? My senses tell me
this guy is pretty attractive.

322
00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:33.000
- Toph!
- Someone else confirmed.

323
00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:34.000
This is serious.

324
00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:36.000
What does "attractive" even mean?

325
00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:37.000
Just give me a straight confirmation.

326
00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:38.000
Is he attractive?

327
00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:39.000
He's very attractive.

328
00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:41.000
Huh?

329
00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:45.000
What? He is.
It's all in the bone structure.

330
00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:47.000
No.

331
00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:49.000
No!

332
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:50.000
NO!

333
00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:51.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Hey.

334
00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:54.000
Easy. You're safe.

335
00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:57.000
Earthbender!

336
00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:59.000
No, no, no. We're all friends here.

337
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:00.000
It's okay.

338
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Someone woke up on the
wrong side of the mountain.

339
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:06.000
Where is she?

340
00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:08.000
Where is Avatar Sonum?

341
00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:10.000
You knew Sonum?

342
00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:13.000
Who are you?

343
00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.000
I don't know how to explain it,

344
00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:18.000
but you've been asleep for a long time.

345
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:20.000
I'm the Avatar now.

346
00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:22.000
I'm Aang.

347
00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:25.000
If you're the Avatar,

348
00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:28.000
then Sonum.

349
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:34.000
Well, Sonum might be long gone,
but on the bright side,

350
00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:37.000
you woke up at the perfect time.

351
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:39.000
Everyone will be amazed
to see another Airbender.

352
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:43.000
Aang's not the last one anymore.

353
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.000
What do you mean, "last"?

354
00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:47.000
Oh.

355
00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:52.000
The Air Nomads.

356
00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:54.000
They've been wiped out.

357
00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:57.000
There's only me.

358
00:30:58.000 --> 00:31:00.000
No.

359
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.000
Sonum Staff, do you have it?

360
00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:05.000
It's our only hope now.

361
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:07.000
What do you mean?

362
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:09.000
I thought it was a weapon.

363
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:12.000
The staff is no weapon.

364
00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:14.000
It is a gift.

365
00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:21.000
With it, Sonum was able to channel
the vast power of the spirit world.

366
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:25.000
It was this power
that allowed Jirana to flourish.

367
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:28.000
The greatest city in the world,

368
00:31:28.000 --> 00:31:30.000
an Air Nomad utopia,

369
00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:34.000
where Sonum presided
over a golden age of balance,

370
00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:37.000
and where I devoted my life
to serving her.

371
00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:42.000
In return, she raised me up
and used her staff to give me,

372
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:47.000
a lowly non-Bender,
the power to bend the air.

373
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:51.000
I was the first,
but I would not be the last.

374
00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:54.000
She filled the skies
with Airbenders,

375
00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:58.000
and we flew by her side,
spreading peace across the world.

376
00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:09.000
Aang, are you okay?

377
00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:14.000
Sonum used the staff
to give people Airbending.

378
00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:17.000
If we found it,

379
00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:20.000
I could bring Airbending back to the world.

380
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:21.000
This is incredible.

381
00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:25.000
There haven't been Airbenders
for over a hundred years.

382
00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:29.000
This is everything you ever wanted, Aang.

383
00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:34.000
We could heal the greatest atrocity
my nation committed in the war.

384
00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:37.000
This could be the final step
to rebuilding the world.

385
00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:39.000
Not if the Denied get there first.

386
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:42.000
They have the map.

387
00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:43.000
Who are the Denied?

388
00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:45.000
A group of violent non-Benders.

389
00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:46.000
They...

390
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:50.000
they must be after the staff
to give themselves Airbending.

391
00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:52.000
Then there's no time to waste.

392
00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:54.000
There's only one place it could be.

393
00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:55.000
Ready your bison.

394
00:32:55.000 --> 00:32:58.000
We'll need to travel
across the endless ocean.

395
00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:00.000
On the other side of the world?

396
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.000
But there's nothing out there.

397
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:02.000
There's an island.

398
00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:04.000
The journey will not be easy,

399
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:07.000
but we can make it.

400
00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:09.000
Then let's get going.

401
00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:12.000
The skies are no place for a water child.

402
00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:14.000
Water child?

403
00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:18.000
Um, I know you just
woke up after thousands of years,

404
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.000
but we do these things together.

405
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:21.000
Trust me,

406
00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:22.000
we're stronger this way.

407
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:25.000
Welcome to Team Avatar.

408
00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:27.000
What's your name?

409
00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:28.000
Taga.

410
00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:31.000
My name is Taga.

411
00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:43.000
Just think of it as a big metal air bison.

412
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:55.000
We will travel ancient
paths through the sky,

413
00:33:55.000 --> 00:33:59.000
ones that our people learned
by following the great air bison herds

414
00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:02.000
that long ago taught us Airbending.

415
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.000
Air currents known only to us,

416
00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:08.000
encircling the great sphere of existence,

417
00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:11.000
allowing us to travel where we wish,

418
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:16.000
giving us our name,
the Air Nomads.

419
00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:46.000
What's he doing?

420
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.000
He's really feeling that air.

421
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:51.000
He's navigating by instinct.

422
00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:54.000
What if his instincts are just wrong?

423
00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:56.000
Who needs instincts
when you've got muscles like that?

424
00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:59.000
Or what if his brain is messed up
from being frozen?

425
00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:00.000
Like me?

426
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.000
Uh, no, no!

427
00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:05.000
He was frozen for 5.000 years, okay?

428
00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:07.000
You were frozen for, what, 100?

429
00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:08.000
Okay, that's nothing.

430
00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:10.000
Your brain is...

431
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:11.000
fresh.

432
00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:15.000
Maybe he is a little
old-fashioned, but look at him.

433
00:35:15.000 --> 00:35:16.000
He's so in tune with his element,

434
00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:22.000
he can travel across the entire ocean
with no map, no instruments.

435
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:27.000
There's so much I can learn from him.

436
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:43.000
I'd give anything to be able
to see my air bison again.

437
00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:47.000
And now,

438
00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:49.000
to see only one remains.

439
00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:53.000
Aang.

440
00:35:53.000 --> 00:35:55.000
You said our people
were wiped out,

441
00:35:55.000 --> 00:35:57.000
yet you survived.

442
00:35:57.000 --> 00:35:59.000
How?

443
00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.000
I had just found out
I was the Avatar,

444
00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:06.000
but the responsibility...

445
00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:08.000
it was too much.

446
00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:11.000
So I ran away.

447
00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:13.000
And while I was gone,

448
00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:16.000
the Fire Nation attacked.

449
00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:20.000
They were looking for me.

450
00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:22.000
If...

451
00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:25.000
If I'd just been there...

452
00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:26.000
Sonum would say,

453
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:30.000
Air nomads are formed
from the mist.

454
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.000
We walk the world
for a moment in time.

455
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:37.000
Then we return
to the eternal wind.

456
00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:40.000
Monkiatsu taught me that.

457
00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:42.000
We carry the same weight,

458
00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:45.000
a grief no one else could
possibly comprehend.

459
00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:49.000
But you and I can heal the past.

460
00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:52.000
Let me show you how powerful
our element can be

461
00:36:52.000 --> 00:36:56.000
when airbenders work together.

462
00:36:58.000 --> 00:37:01.000
What are you doing?!

463
00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:03.000
This is how Sonum taught me!

464
00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:06.000
Feel the energy that tethers us.

465
00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:12.000
The bond between us...

466
00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:14.000
can you feel it?

467
00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:15.000
Use it!

468
00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:18.000
This is amazing!

469
00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:23.000
Whoo-hoo!

470
00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:24.000
Oh, yeah!

471
00:37:24.000 --> 00:37:26.000
Human boomerang!

472
00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:27.000
He's actually flying.

473
00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:28.000
So are we.

474
00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:32.000
Whoa! That's my best friend!
That's my best friend!

475
00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:35.000
No, you throw me!

476
00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:04.000
I had no idea this was possible!

477
00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:07.000
This is only the beginning.

478
00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:16.000
I can't believe it.

479
00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.000
Airbenders will fill the sky again.

480
00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:21.000
We have been given a great gift...

481
00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:23.000
the chance to redeem ourselves.

482
00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:27.000
You were destined to find
me on that mountain, Aang.

483
00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:30.000
How did you end up there?

484
00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:37.000
The earthbenders had attacked Tirana.

485
00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:40.000
Sonum and I fought
fearlessly, side by side.

486
00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:42.000
We drove them back to Mount Bahu,

487
00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:45.000
and that's the last I remember.

488
00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:48.000
She must have saved your life.

489
00:38:48.000 --> 00:38:52.000
Only an Avatar could
have put you in that sphere.

490
00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:58.000
Aang, can I ask you something?

491
00:38:58.000 --> 00:38:59.000
Of course.

492
00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:03.000
If the Fire Nation
destroyed the Air Nomads,

493
00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:07.000
how can you suffer the
presence of the Fire Lord?

494
00:39:09.000 --> 00:39:11.000
Zuko is a friend and an ally.

495
00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:15.000
He turned against his own
father to help me end the war.

496
00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:18.000
Yet he wears the crown himself now.

497
00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:22.000
Fire, by its nature, burns, Aang.

498
00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:26.000
Our kind have always suffered
at the hands of the other elements.

499
00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:29.000
That's why we built Republic City...

500
00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:32.000
to show the world that
if we listen to each other,

501
00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:35.000
we can all live together in peace.

502
00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:38.000
And once we bring back airbenders,

503
00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:41.000
it'll be complete.

504
00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:45.000
When everyone stuck to their own,

505
00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:49.000
the whole world was nearly torn apart.

506
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:53.000
And besides, Katara,
Sokka, Zuko, Toph,

507
00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
they're my family now.

508
00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:59.000
I want to live in a world
where we can all be together.

509
00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:04.000
You remind me so much of Sonum.

510
00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:09.000
It's the Avatar.

511
00:40:09.000 --> 00:40:11.000
And this time,
he's got his friends with them.

512
00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:13.000
That's the Fire Lord's airship.

513
00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:14.000
How'd they get ahead of us?

514
00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:16.000
They don't even have the map.

515
00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:18.000
We can't risk him
getting to the staff first.

516
00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:19.000
Kill him.

517
00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:21.000
But he spared our lives.

518
00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:25.000
And how many Countless were killed in
the hundred years waiting for his return?

519
00:40:25.000 --> 00:40:28.000
Where was he when
your family was wiped out?

520
00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:33.000
If we want anything to change,
we need what the benders have... power.

521
00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:42.000
Fire!

522
00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:50.000
It's the Denied.

523
00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:54.000
Uh, we are definitely under attack.

524
00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:58.000
Turn up your spreads.

525
00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:12.000
Is he crushing the ship?

526
00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:15.000
Taga?

527
00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:17.000
Taga, stop!

528
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:44.000
We're here.

529
00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:47.000
The Immortal Storm.

530
00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:50.000
Oh, no.

531
00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:56.000
There has to be another way around.

532
00:41:56.000 --> 00:41:59.000
No. Together,
you and I can clear a path for the ship.

533
00:41:59.000 --> 00:42:01.000
But we have to go now.

534
00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:04.000
Aang, trust me.

535
00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:09.000
Uh, maybe now's a good time to turn back.

536
00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:12.000
I don't think that's an option anymore.

537
00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:14.000
Where are they going?

538
00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:25.000
The engine's out.
We're losing air pressure.

539
00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:31.000
Katara, come with me.

540
00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:32.000
What about me?

541
00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:33.000
Take the wheel.

542
00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:37.000
What? I've only ever
crashed Fire Nation airships.

543
00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:39.000
Okay, let's see.
Here's our rudder.

544
00:42:39.000 --> 00:42:41.000
This is the elevator.
There's our ballast.

545
00:42:41.000 --> 00:42:45.000
And there's the giant tornado
that's going to kill us all.

546
00:42:47.000 --> 00:42:49.000
Follow my lead.

547
00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.000
Work with me.

548
00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:03.000
Just like I showed you.

549
00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:05.000
We can heart it.

550
00:43:14.000 --> 00:43:18.000
Yes! That's it, Aang.
Keep going.

551
00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:31.000
Got it.

552
00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:36.000
Zuko! Zuko!

553
00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:39.000
Aang and Taga are destroying tornadoes,
but there's too many!

554
00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:40.000
And they're everywhere!

555
00:43:40.000 --> 00:43:41.000
Just steer the ship.

556
00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:42.000
Don't lose Aang.

557
00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:46.000
It's not that easy,
especially when everything is sideways.

558
00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:49.000
Okay, left!

559
00:43:57.000 --> 00:43:59.000
I did it!

560
00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:01.000
Right!

561
00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:11.000
Oh no, we're falling behind!

562
00:44:11.000 --> 00:44:13.000
I'm losing sight of them.

563
00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:14.000
We have to go back.

564
00:44:14.000 --> 00:44:16.000
Trust in your friends.

565
00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:19.000
They won't make it
if we don't clear a path.

566
00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:33.000
Zuko, we're going to crash into the sea!

567
00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:37.000
When I give you the signal,
pull the lever next to the wheel.

568
00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:43.000
We're going to crash!
We're going to crash!

569
00:44:43.000 --> 00:44:45.000
Katara?

570
00:45:04.000 --> 00:45:07.000
Give me the signal!
Give me the signal!

571
00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:13.000
Closed!

572
00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:15.000
Sokka, now!

573
00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:17.000
Here we go!

574
00:45:39.000 --> 00:45:42.000
Katara! We did it!

575
00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:43.000
What were you thinking?

576
00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:45.000
I was clearing the tornadoes
to make a path.

577
00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:48.000
The ship almost crashed, Aang.
We could have died.

578
00:45:48.000 --> 00:45:51.000
And what if you got yourself killed?
You're the Avatar.

579
00:45:51.000 --> 00:45:54.000
This is too risky.
We need to turn back now.

580
00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:55.000
No!

581
00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:56.000
We're almost there.

582
00:45:56.000 --> 00:45:59.000
We just need to get
to the eye of the storm.

583
00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:01.000
Aang, no!

584
00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:02.000
This is too dangerous.

585
00:46:02.000 --> 00:46:04.000
The staff is out there.

586
00:46:04.000 --> 00:46:05.000
They denied her after it.

587
00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:08.000
Do you really believe that they
could make it through the storm?

588
00:46:08.000 --> 00:46:11.000
We're nearly there.
That staff can bring back my people.

589
00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:12.000
I understand how much you want that, but...

590
00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:16.000
You don't understand.
None of you do.

591
00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:18.000
Aang...

592
00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:22.000
We push forward.

593
00:46:24.000 --> 00:46:28.000
If we generate enough air,
we can push our way through.

594
00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:14.000
We're alive?

595
00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:15.000
We made it through.

596
00:47:15.000 --> 00:47:17.000
Thank you, Taga.

597
00:47:17.000 --> 00:47:19.000
It was you, Aang.
We're here because of you.

598
00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:21.000
Yeah, we're having a good time, too.

599
00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:24.000
You could have told us we were
flying into the Immortal Storm.

600
00:47:24.000 --> 00:47:27.000
I know it was dangerous but,
we had to risk it.

601
00:47:27.000 --> 00:47:28.000
We?

602
00:47:28.000 --> 00:47:30.000
I don't remember
when we took a vote on that.

603
00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.000
There wasn't time.
I had to make a call.

604
00:47:32.000 --> 00:47:34.000
Friends, please, don't blame Aang.

605
00:47:34.000 --> 00:47:36.000
This is all my fault.

606
00:47:36.000 --> 00:47:38.000
I knew this would be difficult.

607
00:47:38.000 --> 00:47:41.000
But Aang believed in
your strength as a team.

608
00:47:41.000 --> 00:47:44.000
And I'm honored to be a part of it.

609
00:47:49.000 --> 00:47:51.000
I forgive you, Taga.

610
00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:54.000
Everyone, look.

611
00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:56.000
These islands...

612
00:47:56.000 --> 00:47:57.000
they were...

613
00:47:57.000 --> 00:47:59.000
lion turtles.

614
00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:02.000
Whoa!

615
00:48:03.000 --> 00:48:05.000
It's beautiful.

616
00:48:06.000 --> 00:48:08.000
Long before my time,

617
00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:13.000
the lion turtles granted the
gift of bending to humans.

618
00:48:13.000 --> 00:48:16.000
These are their final resting grounds.

619
00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:20.000
This is where Sonum
came to learn their ways.

620
00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:23.000
I am certain that she left her staff here.

621
00:48:23.000 --> 00:48:25.000
Where should we start looking?

622
00:48:25.000 --> 00:48:28.000
Aang, you must connect with her.

623
00:48:29.000 --> 00:48:32.000
But no one can connect with Sonum.

624
00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:36.000
The spiritual power of the lion
turtles is still concentrated here.

625
00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:37.000
Let it guide you.

626
00:48:37.000 --> 00:48:39.000
We'll set out immediately.

627
00:48:39.000 --> 00:48:42.000
Actually, Taga,
we could really use your help here.

628
00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:45.000
If the denied are close behind,
we need to be ready.

629
00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:49.000
Yeah, and we're gonna need more
than Toph's metal bending to fix this.

630
00:48:49.000 --> 00:48:52.000
My bending got us through that storm.
What did you do?

631
00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:54.000
Steered with his feet.

632
00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:56.000
Repairs can wait. Aang needs me.

633
00:48:56.000 --> 00:49:01.000
Taga, please,
stay and help my friends.

634
00:49:01.000 --> 00:49:03.000
I'll be okay on my own.

635
00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:05.000
As you wish.

636
00:49:05.000 --> 00:49:09.000
We will begin repairs
for our voyage home.

637
00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:13.000
Everyone, I know I've asked
a lot of you on this journey.

638
00:49:13.000 --> 00:49:18.000
But we're about to accomplish
something that will change the world.

639
00:50:08.000 --> 00:50:11.000
"Let it guide you".

640
00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:29.000
Sonum?

641
00:50:46.000 --> 00:50:50.000
Oh, this is turning out
to be a nice little vacation.

642
00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:54.000
Aside from all the people trying
to kill us, and the tornadoes.

643
00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:56.000
Um, we're supposed
to be fixing the ship?

644
00:50:56.000 --> 00:50:58.000
You're doing great, buddy.

645
00:50:58.000 --> 00:51:00.000
Has anyone seen Taga?

646
00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:03.000
Yes, we've all seen Taga.
He's so gorgeous.

647
00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:05.000
Geez, I get it.

648
00:51:05.000 --> 00:51:07.000
Oh, I see what you mean.

649
00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:08.000
He wandered off that way.

650
00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:12.000
No, maybe that way?

651
00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:46.000
Taga?

652
00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:48.000
Where are you going?

653
00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:50.000
Aang needs to be protected.

654
00:51:50.000 --> 00:51:52.000
I agree.

655
00:51:54.000 --> 00:51:57.000
I know my ways may seem unusual to you.

656
00:51:57.000 --> 00:52:01.000
But I assure you,
everything I do, I do for Aang.

657
00:52:01.000 --> 00:52:03.000
For Aang?

658
00:52:03.000 --> 00:52:05.000
Or for the staff?

659
00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:08.000
You have no idea all that we've lost.

660
00:52:08.000 --> 00:52:11.000
You've never known a world
with airbenders.

661
00:52:11.000 --> 00:52:13.000
I know Aang.

662
00:52:13.000 --> 00:52:16.000
He may be the last of his kind.

663
00:52:16.000 --> 00:52:19.000
But he's the reason this world knows peace.

664
00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:27.000
His values as an air nomad
have brought balance to chaos.

665
00:52:28.000 --> 00:52:31.000
It's because of Aang
that the Water Tribes,

666
00:52:31.000 --> 00:52:35.000
Earth Kingdom,
and Fire Nation now work together.

667
00:52:35.000 --> 00:52:37.000
Striving for harmony.

668
00:52:37.000 --> 00:52:41.000
A peace we once thought unattainable.

669
00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:44.000
You speak of peace.

670
00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:47.000
There will never be
peace among the elements.

671
00:52:47.000 --> 00:52:48.000
There never was.

672
00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:52.000
Your precious Republic City
is built on lies.

673
00:52:52.000 --> 00:52:54.000
It's built on hope.

674
00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:56.000
Do you have hope, Taga?

675
00:52:56.000 --> 00:52:59.000
Saving my people requires
more than just hope.

676
00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:01.000
It requires sacrifice.

677
00:53:01.000 --> 00:53:04.000
I saw you try to crush
the denied's airships.

678
00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:06.000
You were ready to kill them.

679
00:53:07.000 --> 00:53:11.000
I know what kind
of airbender Aang is.

680
00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:16.000
But what kind of airbender are you?

681
00:53:43.000 --> 00:53:46.000
Aang did well getting us here.

682
00:53:46.000 --> 00:53:50.000
There is great strength in him,
but weakness as well.

683
00:53:50.000 --> 00:53:51.000
Weakness?

684
00:53:51.000 --> 00:53:54.000
Yes, you.

685
00:54:10.000 --> 00:54:12.000
What the hog monkey?

686
00:54:15.000 --> 00:54:17.000
No!

687
00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:37.000
He trusted you.

688
00:54:43.000 --> 00:54:45.000
No.

689
00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:07.000
Brother.

690
00:56:09.000 --> 00:56:12.000
Taga, it's real.

691
00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:19.000
We can finally bring back airbending.

692
00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:23.000
Let's go tell the others.

693
00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:27.000
We can do this, me and you.

694
00:56:27.000 --> 00:56:30.000
I can't do this without my friends.

695
00:56:31.000 --> 00:56:34.000
Earth killed my people,
fire killed yours.

696
00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:38.000
The staff is the only way
we can create a new air empire.

697
00:56:38.000 --> 00:56:40.000
One capable of defending itself.

698
00:56:40.000 --> 00:56:44.000
No, we can build a new future, Taga.

699
00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:46.000
But it has to be for everyone.

700
00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:48.000
The staff doesn't belong to everyone.

701
00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:49.000
It belongs to us.

702
00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:51.000
What have you done?

703
00:56:51.000 --> 00:56:55.000
As long as they were around,
you always put them ahead of our people.

704
00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:56.000
Don't you see?

705
00:56:56.000 --> 00:56:59.000
This is how we redeem ourselves.

706
00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:01.000
It doesn't matter that you ran then.

707
00:57:01.000 --> 00:57:03.000
As long as you stand with me now.

708
00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:04.000
No.

709
00:57:04.000 --> 00:57:05.000
Aang, listen to me.

710
00:57:05.000 --> 00:57:06.000
Katara.

711
00:57:06.000 --> 00:57:08.000
It's the only way.

712
00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:10.000
No.

713
00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:24.000
You're a traitor to your own.

714
00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:26.000
Just like Sonum.

715
00:58:03.000 --> 00:58:07.000
I wanted to do this
with you by my side.

716
00:58:07.000 --> 00:58:12.000
But if I must build a new air empire alone,
so be it.

717
00:58:20.000 --> 00:58:22.000
There's no way in.

718
00:58:22.000 --> 00:58:23.000
We have to turn back.

719
00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:27.000
No, we keep trying to push through.

720
00:58:38.000 --> 00:58:41.000
Sonum staff.

721
00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:42.000
Denied.

722
00:58:42.000 --> 00:58:45.000
The Avatar is dead.

723
00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:48.000
If you wish to build a new world
where you have the power,

724
00:58:48.000 --> 00:58:51.000
I can give it to you.

725
00:59:05.000 --> 00:59:06.000
Appa.

726
00:59:06.000 --> 00:59:10.000
Katara.

727
00:59:11.000 --> 00:59:13.000
Katara.

728
00:59:13.000 --> 00:59:15.000
They're gone.

729
00:59:15.000 --> 00:59:17.000
It's all my fault.

730
00:59:17.000 --> 00:59:19.000
It's always been my fault.

731
00:59:19.000 --> 00:59:22.000
Ever since I ran away.

732
00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:29.000
No Avatar has ever fallen into such
shame as to join me here in my sorrow.

733
00:59:31.000 --> 00:59:33.000
Why do you grieve so, friend?

734
00:59:33.000 --> 00:59:36.000
Avatar Sonum?

735
00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:40.000
Taga murdered my friends.

736
00:59:40.000 --> 00:59:42.000
And now he has the staff.

737
00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:43.000
Taga.

738
00:59:43.000 --> 00:59:44.000
No.

739
00:59:44.000 --> 00:59:45.000
No, I...

740
00:59:45.000 --> 00:59:47.000
I stopped him.

741
00:59:47.000 --> 00:59:49.000
I hide the staff.

742
00:59:49.000 --> 00:59:51.000
What have you done?

743
00:59:51.000 --> 00:59:54.000
You're the one
who gave him airbending.

744
00:59:54.000 --> 00:59:57.000
How could you give power
to a monster?

745
00:59:57.000 --> 01:00:02.000
The Taga I gave bending
to was a different man.

746
01:00:02.000 --> 01:00:05.000
It was a different time.

747
01:00:05.000 --> 01:00:08.000
The airbenders were the
peacekeepers of the four elements.

748
01:00:08.000 --> 01:00:13.000
We used our power to mediate
all conflict with nonviolence.

749
01:00:13.000 --> 01:00:16.000
But we were the fewest in numbers.

750
01:00:16.000 --> 01:00:21.000
For many years, we existed in a
beautiful balance of great prosperity.

751
01:00:21.000 --> 01:00:23.000
But the world began to shift.

752
01:00:23.000 --> 01:00:26.000
The earthbenders formed their own kingdom,

753
01:00:26.000 --> 01:00:29.000
separating from the other elemental tribes.

754
01:00:29.000 --> 01:00:32.000
The balance of the world was at risk.

755
01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:35.000
It was my duty to act.

756
01:00:35.000 --> 01:00:40.000
So I learned how to channel the energy of the
spirit world just as the lion turtles did.

757
01:00:40.000 --> 01:00:43.000
To give people the power of airbending.

758
01:00:43.000 --> 01:00:49.000
My most devout pupil, Taga,
was the first to receive it.

759
01:00:49.000 --> 01:00:54.000
I sent my new peacekeepers out
to help calm the growing unrest.

760
01:00:54.000 --> 01:00:59.000
But they were not prepared
for the brutality of the new earth kingdom.

761
01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:07.000
Taga watched as his brothers
and sisters were all slaughtered.

762
01:01:07.000 --> 01:01:10.000
His heart darkened
by the violence of war.

763
01:01:10.000 --> 01:01:16.000
He now saw everyone
who wasn't an air nomad as the enemy.

764
01:01:16.000 --> 01:01:17.000
Taga begged me to use the staff

765
01:01:17.000 --> 01:01:21.000
to create an army and to kill all
who would do us harm.

766
01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:23.000
I refused.

767
01:01:23.000 --> 01:01:25.000
So he stole it.

768
01:01:25.000 --> 01:01:28.000
When he connected
the staff to the temple,

769
01:01:28.000 --> 01:01:31.000
his energy was so corrupted
by grief and rage

770
01:01:31.000 --> 01:01:35.000
that the power of the
spirit world consumed him.

771
01:01:35.000 --> 01:01:40.000
Taga became something more than human,
too powerful to kill.

772
01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:44.000
It took all my energy
to finally trap him

773
01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:48.000
high above the clouds
and no one would find him.

774
01:01:48.000 --> 01:01:50.000
I reclaimed the staff,

775
01:01:50.000 --> 01:01:53.000
but I was fatally wounded.

776
01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:55.000
Before the earth kingdom
could invade Jirana,

777
01:01:55.000 --> 01:01:59.000
I sent the remaining air nomads
into the mountains.

778
01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:05.000
And I hid my temple in the spirit world
where no one could access its power.

779
01:02:06.000 --> 01:02:08.000
Then I locked the staff away

780
01:02:08.000 --> 01:02:11.000
where only the avatar could find it.

781
01:02:11.000 --> 01:02:15.000
I died hoping that one day

782
01:02:15.000 --> 01:02:20.000
another avatar would create more airbenders
and restore balance to this world.

783
01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:23.000
And that avatar is you, Aang.

784
01:02:23.000 --> 01:02:27.000
You have to get my staff
before Taga connects it to the temple.

785
01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:28.000
There's still time.

786
01:02:28.000 --> 01:02:31.000
Don't let my regret become yours.

787
01:02:31.000 --> 01:02:34.000
My friends and I fought hard
for this peace.

788
01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:37.000
I won't let him start another war.

789
01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:40.000
Help me find a way back.

790
01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:42.000
Sonum?

791
01:02:42.000 --> 01:02:44.000
What's happening?

792
01:02:46.000 --> 01:02:48.000
No! No!

793
01:02:48.000 --> 01:02:50.000
Please! I have to fix this!

794
01:02:50.000 --> 01:02:52.000
This can't be it!
I can't die yet!

795
01:02:52.000 --> 01:02:55.000
Please! Not yet! No!

796
01:02:55.000 --> 01:02:56.000
- Aang?
- Katara?

797
01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:59.000
Come on, Aang! Come on!

798
01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:02.000
Aang! Move up!

799
01:03:02.000 --> 01:03:04.000
Aang!

800
01:03:04.000 --> 01:03:05.000
Katara.

801
01:03:05.000 --> 01:03:07.000
I was so worried.

802
01:03:07.000 --> 01:03:08.000
Aang.

803
01:03:08.000 --> 01:03:10.000
Sokka.

804
01:03:10.000 --> 01:03:12.000
I knew you'd pull through, buddy.

805
01:03:12.000 --> 01:03:13.000
Hey, Aang.

806
01:03:13.000 --> 01:03:14.000
Zuko.

807
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:16.000
Momo.

808
01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:18.000
Welcome back, Twinkle Toes.

809
01:03:18.000 --> 01:03:21.000
Toph, you're okay.

810
01:03:21.000 --> 01:03:22.000
I thought you were all dead.

811
01:03:22.000 --> 01:03:26.000
We were, but Katara saved us.

812
01:03:26.000 --> 01:03:31.000
The spiritual power of these waters
strengthened my healing abilities.

813
01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:36.000
You're incredible, Katara.

814
01:03:36.000 --> 01:03:38.000
Where's Appa?

815
01:03:39.000 --> 01:03:41.000
Taga must have taken him.

816
01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:43.000
I'm sorry.

817
01:03:43.000 --> 01:03:45.000
No.

818
01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:48.000
I can't believe I trusted him.

819
01:03:49.000 --> 01:03:52.000
We'll get through this.

820
01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:55.000
So, let me get this straight.

821
01:03:55.000 --> 01:04:00.000
He's pulling Sonum's temple out of
the spirit world to gain unlimited power?

822
01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:03.000
And let me guess,
you want us to stop him?

823
01:04:03.000 --> 01:04:09.000
Sure. Only problem is your air bro
crushed our ship and stole your bison.

824
01:04:09.000 --> 01:04:13.000
Also, there's a massive
typhoon surrounding us!

825
01:04:15.000 --> 01:04:19.000
I don't say this very often,
but Sokka's right.

826
01:04:19.000 --> 01:04:21.000
- Thank you.
- Yep, we're stuck.

827
01:04:21.000 --> 01:04:24.000
And there aren't enough lion turtles
for all of us to have our own island.

828
01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:27.000
So, I'm calling this one.
I'm naming him Snappy.

829
01:04:27.000 --> 01:04:29.000
Aw, Snappy is the best one.

830
01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:31.000
I know.

831
01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:33.000
We may not know where Taga is,

832
01:04:33.000 --> 01:04:37.000
but we know what he's looking for
is in the spirit world.

833
01:04:37.000 --> 01:04:42.000
And lucky for us, we're stuck in the most
spiritually charged place on the planet.

834
01:04:42.000 --> 01:04:45.000
So, I may be able to open
a portal to get us there,

835
01:04:45.000 --> 01:04:49.000
if I can summon an old friend.

836
01:04:57.000 --> 01:04:59.000
Wow.

837
01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:01.000
The ocean spirit.

838
01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:11.000
This portal smells an awful
lot like the fish market.

839
01:05:11.000 --> 01:05:13.000
I'm gonna go check on Snappy.

840
01:05:13.000 --> 01:05:15.000
Face your death with honor.

841
01:05:15.000 --> 01:05:16.000
I'm sorry.

842
01:05:16.000 --> 01:05:20.000
I know I got us into this,
but I promise you I'll fix it.

843
01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:22.000
We'll fix it.

844
01:05:22.000 --> 01:05:24.000
Together.

845
01:05:27.000 --> 01:05:30.000
We're gonna die! We're gonna die!

846
01:05:39.000 --> 01:05:42.000
What? Where's my power pony?

847
01:05:42.000 --> 01:05:45.000
Were my hands always this small?

848
01:05:45.000 --> 01:05:48.000
It's baby Toph! Baby Toph!

849
01:05:49.000 --> 01:05:51.000
What the hog monkey?

850
01:05:51.000 --> 01:05:52.000
Old people.

851
01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:53.000
Grand.. Grand..?

852
01:05:53.000 --> 01:05:55.000
That's your sister, you weak head!

853
01:05:55.000 --> 01:05:58.000
Give me Toph.
There, there, Toph.

854
01:05:58.000 --> 01:05:59.000
Oh no, Zuko!

855
01:05:59.000 --> 01:06:01.000
What happened
to your beautiful face?

856
01:06:01.000 --> 01:06:04.000
You look like a dried sea squid.

857
01:06:04.000 --> 01:06:06.000
No, Zuko!

858
01:06:06.000 --> 01:06:08.000
What's going on here?

859
01:06:09.000 --> 01:06:11.000
The spirit world is out of balance.

860
01:06:11.000 --> 01:06:13.000
And so are we.

861
01:06:15.000 --> 01:06:18.000
That's gotta be Taga.

862
01:06:38.000 --> 01:06:40.000
Oh no!

863
01:06:40.000 --> 01:06:42.000
He's pulling Sonum temple
into our world!

864
01:06:42.000 --> 01:06:45.000
We're running out of time!

865
01:06:51.000 --> 01:06:53.000
Pretty good landing.

866
01:06:53.000 --> 01:06:57.000
Whoa! Humans! I love humans!

867
01:06:57.000 --> 01:07:00.000
Two brothers, their little sister,
and an elderly couple.

868
01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:01.000
Not a couple!

869
01:07:01.000 --> 01:07:04.000
Whoa!
Looks like I touched a nerve.

870
01:07:04.000 --> 01:07:06.000
Oh, look at this one! Hello!

871
01:07:06.000 --> 01:07:09.000
Toph! No! Bad Toph!

872
01:07:09.000 --> 01:07:11.000
Don't bite strangers.

873
01:07:12.000 --> 01:07:15.000
Great spirit! Excuse me, did you
just come from that temple in the sky?

874
01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:18.000
I certainly did.

875
01:07:18.000 --> 01:07:19.000
It was my favorite hidey hole.

876
01:07:19.000 --> 01:07:23.000
Until that dark, yucky energy
started corrupting this whole place.

877
01:07:23.000 --> 01:07:26.000
Please, we need your help getting up there.

878
01:07:26.000 --> 01:07:29.000
It's my duty to stop this.

879
01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:31.000
I'm the Avatar.

880
01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:35.000
Ooh! The Avatar!

881
01:07:35.000 --> 01:07:36.000
Let me have a squiz at you.

882
01:07:36.000 --> 01:07:38.000
Okay, now with this eye.

883
01:07:38.000 --> 01:07:39.000
And this eye.

884
01:07:39.000 --> 01:07:41.000
Ooh, don't forget this eye.

885
01:07:41.000 --> 01:07:42.000
Can we hurry it up?

886
01:07:42.000 --> 01:07:43.000
I need to have a squiz.

887
01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:46.000
Sniff check!

888
01:07:47.000 --> 01:07:49.000
Ooh, that's Avatar material right there.

889
01:07:49.000 --> 01:07:52.000
Yes, it is. Oh!

890
01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:53.000
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

891
01:07:53.000 --> 01:07:59.000
It appears the universe has brought
us together for a very important mission.

892
01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:01.000
To flee!

893
01:08:01.000 --> 01:08:03.000
And be alive!

894
01:08:03.000 --> 01:08:05.000
Wait! Come back!

895
01:08:05.000 --> 01:08:06.000
We're going the wrong way!

896
01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:07.000
Stop!

897
01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:10.000
Please, great spirit,
both of our worlds are in danger.

898
01:08:10.000 --> 01:08:11.000
No, no, no, no, no, no.

899
01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:14.000
I am not going back up there.

900
01:08:19.000 --> 01:08:23.000
Hmm, well, when you put it like that,
it does make more sense.

901
01:08:23.000 --> 01:08:27.000
Upon reflection, I've decided I shall
help you and your human-y friends.

902
01:08:27.000 --> 01:08:28.000
What did he say?

903
01:08:28.000 --> 01:08:30.000
Nice work, momo.

904
01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:32.000
Alright, in you go.

905
01:08:35.000 --> 01:08:38.000
By the way, no eating anything you find
in my teeth, as I'm saving that for later.

906
01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:40.000
Ready, set, get steady and rest.

907
01:08:40.000 --> 01:08:44.000
One and the two and
the you know what to do.

908
01:08:44.000 --> 01:08:46.000
Bluff!

909
01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:54.000
I know we haven't known each
other very long, but I love you!

910
01:08:54.000 --> 01:08:57.000
You don't have to say it back.

911
01:09:04.000 --> 01:09:06.000
Hey! You got your hair back!

912
01:09:06.000 --> 01:09:10.000
Why are my eyes cheery?
Was I crying?

913
01:09:10.000 --> 01:09:12.000
No way! Look!

914
01:09:12.000 --> 01:09:13.000
What? What is it?

915
01:09:13.000 --> 01:09:16.000
It's Republic City.

916
01:09:19.000 --> 01:09:22.000
We can't let him destroy
everything we've built.

917
01:09:22.000 --> 01:09:24.000
We won't.

918
01:09:38.000 --> 01:09:40.000
Boomerang!

919
01:09:57.000 --> 01:09:58.000
Give me the staff, Taga!

920
01:09:58.000 --> 01:10:01.000
I see I underestimated you, Avatar.

921
01:10:01.000 --> 01:10:04.000
Your friends are stronger than I thought.

922
01:10:04.000 --> 01:10:07.000
But you're too late.

923
01:10:14.000 --> 01:10:15.000
The Denied.

924
01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:18.000
You see, I did what you wanted, Aang.

925
01:10:18.000 --> 01:10:22.000
I returned airbending to the world.

926
01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:24.000
What's the plan?

927
01:10:24.000 --> 01:10:27.000
We'll deal with the Denied.
You have to get the staff.

928
01:10:27.000 --> 01:10:32.000
I will rebuild Geronimo and the ruins
of our enemies, just as they did on ours.

929
01:10:32.000 --> 01:10:35.000
A new air empire will rise.

930
01:10:35.000 --> 01:10:38.000
Kill them all.

931
01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:58.000
We have to get these people out of here.

932
01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:04.000
Whoa!

933
01:11:14.000 --> 01:11:16.000
Oh, yeah.

934
01:11:22.000 --> 01:11:26.000
Taga! Give it to me!

935
01:11:27.000 --> 01:11:28.000
This isn't the way.

936
01:11:28.000 --> 01:11:31.000
We can use the staff
to bring back the balance.

937
01:11:31.000 --> 01:11:36.000
You care so much about your ideals
that you'd let your people die!

938
01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:40.000
I will do anything
to make sure they survive!

939
01:11:57.000 --> 01:12:00.000
My cabbages! My cabbages!

940
01:12:05.000 --> 01:12:07.000
My cabbages...!

941
01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:11.000
My cabbages!

942
01:12:24.000 --> 01:12:25.000
Don't do this.

943
01:12:25.000 --> 01:12:26.000
You have the power now.

944
01:12:26.000 --> 01:12:28.000
You can decide how to use it.

945
01:12:28.000 --> 01:12:29.000
I'm not like you.

946
01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:31.000
The world hasn't been good to me.

947
01:12:31.000 --> 01:12:32.000
The world is what we make it.

948
01:12:32.000 --> 01:12:35.000
Get away from her!

949
01:13:06.000 --> 01:13:08.000
Taga! Stop!

950
01:13:12.000 --> 01:13:15.000
You betrayed me!
You betrayed our culture!

951
01:13:15.000 --> 01:13:18.000
I gave you every chance
to see the truth!

952
01:13:23.000 --> 01:13:27.000
Can you be in the Fire Nation?

953
01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:31.000
I'm fighting for the peace of all nations.

954
01:13:34.000 --> 01:13:38.000
Big talk from someone who sits
on a throne built on a century of war!

955
01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:05.000
I'm still the greatest
earthbender in the world!

956
01:14:28.000 --> 01:14:29.000
Oh no!

957
01:14:29.000 --> 01:14:31.000
I'm out of water!

958
01:14:33.000 --> 01:14:34.000
We got ya!

959
01:14:34.000 --> 01:14:38.000
And there's no Avatar here
to save you.

960
01:14:39.000 --> 01:14:42.000
Suck a cycle!

961
01:14:44.000 --> 01:14:50.000
Let's see if your fancy new bending
can beat some good ol' non-bending know-how!

962
01:14:56.000 --> 01:14:59.000
He comes away!

963
01:15:04.000 --> 01:15:07.000
You just got denied!

964
01:15:14.000 --> 01:15:15.000
Let's go!

965
01:15:15.000 --> 01:15:19.000
Good luck saving your city!

966
01:15:26.000 --> 01:15:29.000
We have to save as many people as we can!

967
01:15:46.000 --> 01:15:48.000
I know your pain.

968
01:15:48.000 --> 01:15:51.000
I know what you've been through.

969
01:15:51.000 --> 01:15:53.000
You don't know.

970
01:15:53.000 --> 01:15:58.000
I watched as all of my brothers
and sisters were slaughtered.

971
01:15:58.000 --> 01:16:02.000
And the Fire Nation burned
the Air Nomads to ash!

972
01:16:02.000 --> 01:16:04.000
Where were you?

973
01:16:04.000 --> 01:16:06.000
You ran!

974
01:16:26.000 --> 01:16:28.000
Taga!

975
01:16:37.000 --> 01:16:39.000
No!

976
01:17:01.000 --> 01:17:06.000
The full power of the Spirit World
flows through me!

977
01:17:15.000 --> 01:17:19.000
This is what strength looks like!

978
01:18:12.000 --> 01:18:17.000
You should've run away like you
did all those years ago, little Avatar.

979
01:18:17.000 --> 01:18:20.000
I...

980
01:18:20.000 --> 01:18:21.000
won't...

981
01:18:21.000 --> 01:18:26.000
Then at least you'll die knowing
you're not the last Airbender!

982
01:19:03.000 --> 01:19:05.000
Aang...

983
01:19:12.000 --> 01:19:14.000
No!

984
01:20:20.000 --> 01:20:23.000
We could've been brothers!

985
01:20:23.000 --> 01:20:25.000
We could've done this together!

986
01:20:25.000 --> 01:20:28.000
It didn't have to end like this!

987
01:20:32.000 --> 01:20:34.000
It's Aang. He's got the staff!

988
01:20:34.000 --> 01:20:36.000
Yeah! Kick his butt, Mega Aang!

989
01:20:36.000 --> 01:20:38.000
No! Something's wrong!

990
01:20:38.000 --> 01:20:41.000
The power is corrupting him!

991
01:20:48.000 --> 01:20:50.000
No!

992
01:20:58.000 --> 01:21:02.000
I dreamt of bringing the Air Nomads
back to the world as peacekeepers.

993
01:21:02.000 --> 01:21:06.000
They could've been a beacon
of light for the world to follow.

994
01:21:06.000 --> 01:21:07.000
But you ruined it!

995
01:21:07.000 --> 01:21:10.000
You twisted my dream
into a nightmare!

996
01:21:10.000 --> 01:21:11.000
Finally.

997
01:21:11.000 --> 01:21:14.000
You have the power
the Air Nomads need.

998
01:21:14.000 --> 01:21:17.000
Maybe there is hope
for you after all.

999
01:21:27.000 --> 01:21:28.000
Do it!

1000
01:21:28.000 --> 01:21:30.000
Use the staff!

1001
01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:34.000
Show me you have the strength to bring
our people back!

1002
01:21:34.000 --> 01:21:36.000
Do it!

1003
01:22:12.000 --> 01:22:14.000
Aang...

1004
01:22:16.000 --> 01:22:19.000
You will do so many
great things as the Avatar.

1005
01:22:19.000 --> 01:22:24.000
But you must be prepared
to do what frightens you the most.

1006
01:22:25.000 --> 01:22:30.000
Your people, your home,
we are always with you.

1007
01:22:46.000 --> 01:22:48.000
No!

1008
01:22:53.000 --> 01:22:55.000
No...

1009
01:23:18.000 --> 01:23:19.000
No!

1010
01:23:19.000 --> 01:23:21.000
My power!

1011
01:23:27.000 --> 01:23:30.000
No. No!

1012
01:23:39.000 --> 01:23:42.000
You fool! Why?

1013
01:23:42.000 --> 01:23:45.000
Why did you break it?

1014
01:23:45.000 --> 01:23:48.000
We could've fixed everything.

1015
01:23:48.000 --> 01:23:52.000
We can't erase the pain of the past.

1016
01:23:52.000 --> 01:23:54.000
We couldn't save them.

1017
01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:58.000
But it's our duty
to protect our people.

1018
01:23:58.000 --> 01:24:01.000
Not at the cost of betraying
everything they stood for.

1019
01:24:01.000 --> 01:24:03.000
No.

1020
01:24:03.000 --> 01:24:05.000
It's time to let go.

1021
01:24:05.000 --> 01:24:08.000
You have to forgive yourself.

1022
01:24:10.000 --> 01:24:13.000
I have to forgive myself too.

1023
01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:25.000
Air Nomads are formed from the best.

1024
01:24:28.000 --> 01:24:33.000
We walk the world
for a moment in time.

1025
01:24:34.000 --> 01:24:39.000
Then we return
to the eternal wind.

1026
01:24:54.000 --> 01:24:57.000
Aang!

1027
01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:01.000
Hey, Katara.

1028
01:25:01.000 --> 01:25:03.000
Hey, Aang.

1029
01:25:05.000 --> 01:25:06.000
Seriously?

1030
01:25:06.000 --> 01:25:09.000
You do realize you're falling, right?

1031
01:25:09.000 --> 01:25:11.000
Hey, if you ever get
tired of relying on Appa,

1032
01:25:11.000 --> 01:25:15.000
I can hook you up with
one of these babies.

1033
01:25:18.000 --> 01:25:21.000
I'll give you the best friend discount!

1034
01:25:35.000 --> 01:25:38.000
I don't know if
airbending will ever return.

1035
01:25:38.000 --> 01:25:41.000
But I know now that the
true power of the Air Nomads

1036
01:25:41.000 --> 01:25:43.000
was never their bending.

1037
01:25:43.000 --> 01:25:45.000
It was their values.

1038
01:25:45.000 --> 01:25:48.000
And that's a power
I can pass on to others.

1039
01:25:49.000 --> 01:25:50.000
Avatar Aang,

1040
01:25:50.000 --> 01:25:55.000
you are the true embodiment
of the Air Nomads.

1041
01:25:55.000 --> 01:25:59.000
Thank you for giving up
the power that I could not.

1042
01:25:59.000 --> 01:26:02.000
You give me hope
for the future of our culture.

1043
01:26:15.000 --> 01:26:18.000
It's amazing, isn't it?

1044
01:26:18.000 --> 01:26:22.000
The first new air temple
in centuries.

1045
01:26:22.000 --> 01:26:26.000
Republic City is finally complete.

1046
01:26:29.000 --> 01:26:33.000
A city for all nations,
just like you promised.

1047
01:26:33.000 --> 01:26:36.000
I never could have done
this without you, Katara.

1048
01:26:37.000 --> 01:26:40.000
Hey, everybody.
Sorry I kept you all waiting.

1049
01:26:40.000 --> 01:26:43.000
Are you ready for our big trip?

1050
01:26:43.000 --> 01:26:45.000
As my new acolytes,

1051
01:26:45.000 --> 01:26:49.000
you'll be helping me preserve
our culture for future generations.

1052
01:26:49.000 --> 01:26:54.000
So, who wants to search for artifacts
at an ancient abandoned temple?

1053
01:26:54.000 --> 01:26:55.000
Yay.

1054
01:26:55.000 --> 01:26:59.000
I'm only going to make sure you don't
try to release another beefy old airbender.

1055
01:26:59.000 --> 01:27:02.000
Yeah, I'm done with bad boys.

1056
01:27:13.000 --> 01:27:16.000
Avatar Sonum told me about this place,

1057
01:27:16.000 --> 01:27:20.000
so it's very possible that no one's
been here in hundreds of years.

1058
01:27:21.000 --> 01:27:24.000
Oh, is this an airbender relic?

1059
01:27:24.000 --> 01:27:26.000
I think that's just a rock.

1060
01:27:26.000 --> 01:27:28.000
But I love the enthusiasm.

1061
01:27:29.000 --> 01:27:31.000
Oh.

1062
01:27:33.000 --> 01:27:35.000
Keep your eyes open.

1063
01:27:35.000 --> 01:27:37.000
You never know
what we might discover here.

1064
01:27:38.000 --> 01:27:40.000
Wouh.

1065
